// The Scared Townperson of Millhaven: the goblin raid quest, before and after.

== hub
npc: I don't get many friendly faces through here anymore.  #smile  #line:f3c988
npc: Watch yourself. Even standing here talking to you, I keep expecting something to come out of the trees.  #wary  #close  #line:cc00a1
npc: What did you want to know?  #neutral  #line:4a272e
* [noflag townsperson_heard_raids] What's been happening around here?  #line:f17856
    set townsperson_heard_raids
    -> quest_intro
* Tell me about this town.  #line:3b31d9
    -> town
* What are the people like, around here?  #line:d22c10
    -> people
* What's day-to-day life like for you?  #line:867ae2
    -> life
* I should get going. Take care.  #line:b30da7


== quest_intro
before: [present DwarfFighter] -> quest_intro_dwarf_reaction
npc: You mean the raids.  #frown  #line:d3c313
npc: Goblins, mostly. Small bands, quick and mean.  #line:123bd0
npc: But there's bigger ones running with them now. Uglier, smarter, giving the orders.  #close  #line:4fc078
npc: It's gotten worse these past few months.  #line:f508e8
* What exactly have they done?  #line:977488
    give healing_potion
    -> quest_details
* [passive Insight] If you aren't telling me everything, please do so.  #line:d6ba6c
    -> quest_insight
* [Light] That's terrible. I hope it gets better.  #line:e5aa21
    -> hub
* [Dark] Rough. But that's not really my problem.  #line:eec54c
    -> hub


== quest_intro_dwarf_reaction
DwarfFighter: Whatever's got her this rattled, we should hear her out.  #frown  #line:f2dd1e
-> quest_intro


== quest_details
npc: Three nights back they hit the Hollis farm.  #frown  #line:799f7a
npc: Burned the grain store, took what livestock they could herd off.  #line:c72b93
npc: Put an arrow through Old Hollis's leg when he came out swinging a torch at them.  #close  #line:19a770
npc: Before that it was the mill. Before that, some fool who wandered too close to the tree line at dusk never came home at all.  #wary  #line:f5dc44
npc: They don't come every night. Just enough that nobody sleeps easy anymore.  #line:05a561
* Do you know where they're camped?  #line:c5f7f4
    -> quest_location
* [contest Persuasion vs Insight] Push her for exactly where they're camped.  #line:4f8f5d
    say: You know more than you're saying. Where exactly are they camped?  #line:a24678
    success -> quest_location
    failure -> quest_pushed_back
* I'll keep an eye out.  #line:06efe4
    -> potion_gift


== quest_insight
npc: ...There's one more thing.  #wary  #close  #line:b2d814
npc: The night they hit the mill, I saw one of them stop at the well and just stare at it. Like it was looking for something.  #line:332a06
npc: The others didn't seem to notice, but the big one did. It got angry, herded it along.  #line:1d2593
npc: I haven't told anyone that part. Didn't want people thinking I'd lost my nerve completely.  #frown  #line:0280c7
-> quest_details


== quest_location
npc: Somewhere out past the old quarry, if I had to guess.  #neutral  #line:246b8a
npc: That's the direction they always come from, and where the tracks lead back to.  #line:f73fa1
npc: Nobody from town's been foolish enough to go look.  #line:00fdf1
npc: If you're thinking about it... just be careful. Please.  #frown  #close  #line:b0c54a
-> potion_gift


== quest_pushed_back
npc: I've told you what I know. Don't push me on this.  #angry  #close  #line:4fc3d6
-> potion_gift


== potion_gift
npc: Here, take this. I hope it helps if you encounter them.  #smile  #line:9d8c40
-> hub


== town
npc: This is Millhaven. Or what's left of the name, anyway.  #line:e839b7
npc: Used to be a proper stop on the trade road, back when the road was worth traveling.  #line:86dbee
npc: There's the mill, the old chapel, maybe two dozen houses worth calling homes.  #line:80f6d8
npc: Half the storefronts on the square have been shuttered since the raids started. Folks who could afford to leave, did.  #line:daa54b
-> hub


== people
npc: Stubborn, mostly. That's what's kept this place standing as long as it has.  #line:cc6b3b
npc: We look out for each other, share what food there is, take turns on the watch at night.  #line:8296c2
npc: There's an old woman, Maren, who's buried two sons to the raids and still bakes bread for anyone who knocks.  #close  #line:920273
npc: That's the kind of people we are. Doesn't mean we're not scared. Just means we haven't left yet.  #line:1d1bed
-> hub


== life
npc: Tiring, if I'm honest.  #line:dc11ca
npc: I used to work the mill during the day and sleep easy at night.  #line:03d8a5
npc: Now I still work the mill, but I take a turn on the watch wall twice a week, and I don't sleep easy any night.  #line:c7a139
npc: You get used to flinching at every sound past dark.  #line:f9b64e
npc: I keep telling myself it won't always be like this. Some days I believe it.  #close  #line:231d89
-> hub


== resolved_hub
npc: They're gone. All of them.  #line:baae8b
npc: No torches on the treeline last night, first time since this started.  #line:986237
npc: I keep waiting to hear something moving out there, and there's nothing.  #line:bb922a
npc: I don't have the words for what you did for this town.  #close  #line:e45c0d
* [noflag goblin_raid.begun] Were those all of them?  #line:7d1e94
    set goblin_raid.begun
    -> raid_warning
* [Lawful] We were glad to help.  #line:a96334
    -> resolved_hub
* [Chaotic] It's what you paid us for.  #line:c4a368
    -> resolved_hub
* Is it really over?  #line:57af74
    -> resolved_reassurance
* Take care of yourself.  #line:951d41


== raid_warning
npc: ...No. That's what's been eating at me.  #line:a84f2b
npc: The quarry crew saw more of them on the road at dawn. A big one, and bows. Heading for the rise.  #line:3c61e7
npc: That's where the crew sleeps, behind that palisade up past the pit. Goblins don't forget a thing like what you did.  #line:e92d50
npc: If they hit anyone back, it'll be the camp. And it'll be tonight.  #close  #line:5b07ac
* Then we go now.  #line:c4f81d
* Keep your doors barred. We'll handle it.  #line:16e3a9


== resolved_reassurance
npc: I think so. I sent word to the mill and the Hollis farm. Nobody's seen so much as a footprint since.  #line:1f6bf5
npc: Doesn't mean I've stopped checking the treeline every morning, but... it's quiet. Really quiet.  #line:a17ca8
-> resolved_hub
